Changelog

v1.20

Fixed
* Double-encoded JSON responses. Delta’s API now returns bodies wrapped in an extra layer of quotes, e.g. "{"Success":true,"Message":""}". Hubitat’s built-in JSON parser rejected this and threw an exception, so toggleWater logged “Error toggling water” even though the faucet actually turned on. The driver now requests the raw text, strips the wrapping quotes, unescapes it, and parses it with JsonSlurper.
* Switch state not updating. A side effect of the parsing exception was that the Hubitat switch state never changed after On/Off. It now updates correctly.
* Wrong event description. sendSwitchState always reported “is off” in the event description, whatever the state. It now reports the actual state ("... is on" or "... is off").

Changed

* httpExec rewritten.
    * Uses textParser: true to bypass Hubitat’s JSON parsing.
    * Returns a normalized result of [status: ..., data: ...], so existing callers (toggleWater, dispense_mL, queryUsageReport) work unchanged.
    * Wraps the request in a try/catch for HttpResponseException, so HTTP errors (401, 403, 404 and so on) now log the actual status code and response body.
    * Calls .trim() on the token to guard against stray whitespace or newlines from pasting.
    * Updates the User-Agent from Chrome/110 to Chrome/131.
* Parse failures are logged. If a response can’t be parsed as JSON, the raw text is logged when debug logging is on, and the raw text is passed through as data.
* Null-safe error logging. response.status became response?.status in the failure branches of queryUsageReport, toggleWater and dispense_mL, so a failed request logs a clean error rather than a null-pointer exception.
* Import enabled. import groovy.json.JsonSlurper is now uncommented.
* Change history. Added a 1.20 entry.
* Whitespace. Tabs were converted to spaces in the command lines in the metadata block.
Added (commented out)
* Two diagnostic log.info lines: one in toggleWater for the response, and one in httpExec for the raw response text. They stay available for future troubleshooting.
Unchanged
* All commands, preferences, dispense unit conversions and the usage refresh() logic, including the dataOffset = 1 setting. The note from earlier still applies: if you want the last full day rather than the current partial day, switch to the commented-out dataOffset line.
Root cause
Delta changed their server’s response format to double-encode JSON.

v1.21

Feature added

* Added Warm Up Water command and required Delta device name preference

v1.22

Fixed

* Added Actuator capability for use in Rule Machine
